This is one of the hardest DP + Bitmask problems on GFG. The trick is that **arr[i] ≤ 30**, which is much more important than **n ≤ 10^5**.

---

# Problem Understanding

You are given an array.

You have to count all subsets such that

> Product of all numbers in that subset can be written as multiplication of **distinct primes only**.

That means

Every prime can appear **at most once** in the final product.

Example

```
6 = 2 × 3      ✅ valid

30 = 2 × 3 × 5 ✅ valid

4 = 2 × 2      ❌ invalid

12 = 2 × 2 × 3 ❌ invalid

18 = 2 × 3 × 3 ❌ invalid

8 = 2 × 2 × 2 ❌ invalid
```

So repeated prime factors are NOT allowed.

