# Why Backward DP?

Suppose

```
dp
```

is updated left-to-right.

Current number

```
2
```

might be added twice in one iteration.

Backward iteration guarantees that each occurrence value (represented by its frequency multiplier) is considered only once per transition, preserving the 0/1 subset property for each distinct value.

